whisper-echo Debian packaging notes
===================================

Build system
------------
The upstream project uses CMake. The Debian package is built with debhelper
compat 13 and CMake via dh_auto_*.

To build:
  dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc

The package does NOT install udev rules automatically. Uinput access is
security sensitive and is left to the administrator. See docs/uinput.md and
share/whisper-echo/setup_uinput.sh for manual setup instructions.

Files
-----
* debian/whisper-echo.manpages – declares the man page
* debian/whisper-echo.docs – declares documentation files
* debian/whisper-echo.install – explicit install list for CMake-built files

Versioning
----------
Version is taken from git tags via CMake. For Debian releases, use
upstream_version-debian_revision, e.g. 0.1.0-1.

Standards
---------
Complies with Debian Policy 4.7.0, no auto-installed udev rules, man page
compressed, docs installed under /usr/share/doc.
